   "text_sha256": "07483e6207ab8a25bd9d857f2a5f03e32f9904004ae82b304946d23ae6bd621a",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file is the package entry point for exllamav3. Before importing torch, it sets `ROCPROFILER_REGISTER_ENABLED=0` by default to avoid a ROCm profiler thread spinning on a core; it then imports torch and raises a helpful error if torch is missing. It also applies default runtime settings: enabling expandable segments for the CUDA caching allocator (skipped on Windows, ROCm, or when the user has configured the allocator), and pointing Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds. Finally, it re-exports the library's main public classes (Config, Model, Tokenizer, Cache, Generator, samplers, etc.) so they can be imported directly from `exllamav3`."
  },
  "8192": {
   "prompt_tokens": 8192,
