   "decode_tok_s": 18.42,
   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "2c68f02f7e8566c6ff670d3b6f17bdb6ddc568db02639ea5a2f44fe50ae44199",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package entry point for exllamav3. It sets environment defaults before importing PyTorch\u2014disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread by default and configuring the CUDA caching allocator with expandable segments (skipping Windows, ROCm, and user-configured cases)\u2014and points Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds. It then imports torch with a helpful error message if torch is missing, and re-exports the library's main public API: `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, cache classes, generator classes, and sampler symbols."
  },
  "32768": {
   "prompt_tokens": 32768,
   "prompt_sha256": "fcc5374c6f0b1a39129148f5fab3c035f332097f59083060b14349bbbd76c4fa",
   "ttft_s": 80.28,
   "prefill_tok_s": 408.1,
