   "decode_tok_s": 17.86,
   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "deb0bfa99b4d2ce8e79e7cdbe9379dda63bafaba623a43dd4bca3a58b9c86d88",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package entry point for exllamav3. It sets environment defaults before importing PyTorch (notably disabling the ROCm profiler registration to avoid a spinning HSA event thread), raises a helpful error if PyTorch is missing, and configures the CUDA caching allocator to use expandable segments unless the user has already set `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF` or is on Windows/ROCm. It also points Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds. Finally, it re-exports the library's main public API\u2014`Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, cache classes, generator/job classes, and sampler symbols\u2014so users can import them directly from `exllamav3`."
  }
